Renderer adjustments for the Switch's Mesa (nouveau) GL 4.3 stack (__SWITCH__).

- XF block words read as a whole uvec4 plus a component select, and the copy
  encoder's divisions by run-time values done in floats with an exact
  correction: same results, without the code Switch emulators (Eden) misread
  or cannot run (gx_shader.cpp, gx_render.cpp)
- matrix rows (R4) and normal rows (R3) read as whole uvec4 loads: the same
  values, and half the GLSL link time per program on the console's Mesa
- the window is the whole display from the start: the Switch's SDL sizes the
  framebuffer once, at creation (gx_platform.cpp)
- the shader warm-up draws once with each program it makes (nothing is
  rasterised), so Mesa's nouveau makes its GPU code during the load instead
  of at the program's first draw in gameplay (gx_shader.cpp)
- the program cache's records are read into memory at the start and made
  into programs (with the same draw) when a stage's warm-up or a draw first
  needs them: making one from its binary costs nearly a compile on the
  console's Mesa, so making all ~850 at the start took longer than the loads
  they save. A record Mesa rejects (another build of it) starts the file over.
  SMS_GX_SHADER_WARMUP_MS sets the warm-up's time for other stages' programs
  (1000000: all known programs, to make a full cache) and
  SMS_GX_SHADER_WARM_DRAW=0 leaves the draws out (gx_shader.cpp)
- the program cache keeps the whole records before a damaged one, and is
  closed and opened again after each stage's warm-up: a game closed from the
  HOME menu leaves its open files at an older size (gx_shader.cpp)
- SMS_TEXTURE_PACKS separated by ';' only: Switch paths begin with a device
  name and a colon (romfs:/textures) (gx_hires.cpp)
- a "switch" button prompt style (SMS_BUTTON_PROMPTS=switch, and automatic
  for Switch Pro Controllers and Joy-Cons), its images in
  SMS_BUTTON_PROMPT_DIR/switch.png as for the other styles (gx_prompts.cpp)
- both sticks pressed together (L3 + R3) toggle the debug overlay, as the
  backtick key does on a PC (gx_platform.cpp)

